<section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-graphite" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="faq-heading"
      index="12"
      label="Frequently Asked Questions"
      title="Common questions about cloud-native engineering."
      lede="Answers to the questions we hear most often from engineering leaders evaluating cloud-native adoption."
      tone="graphite"
    />

    <div class="mt-14 max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-4" data-reveal-group>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is the difference between cloud native and cloud hosted?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Cloud hosted means running applications on rented virtual machines. Cloud native means architecting applications as loosely coupled services that leverage containers, orchestration, automated delivery, and declarative infrastructure. Cloud hosted is where you run. Cloud native is how you build.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How long does a cloud-native migration typically take?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Timelines vary by scope. A single application can be migrated in 4 to 8 weeks. A full enterprise platform transformation typically takes 6 to 18 months. We start with high-value, low-risk workloads to demonstrate results and build momentum.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          Do I need Kubernetes to be cloud native?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">No. Kubernetes is a popular platform substrate, but cloud-native architectures can use serverless functions, container platforms like AWS ECS, or even well-structured monolithic applications. The key is adopting cloud-native principles, not a specific tool.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do containers improve security?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Containers provide isolation, immutable images that can be scanned for vulnerabilities, and a smaller attack surface than traditional VMs. Combined with image signing, runtime security, and network policies, containers improve the security posture significantly.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How much does cloud-native adoption cost?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">The investment depends on your current state and desired outcomes. Most clients see a positive ROI within 6 to 12 months through infrastructure cost reduction, productivity gains, and faster delivery. We provide a business case with projected ROI before any engagement begins.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          Will cloud native improve application performance?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Yes, when done correctly. Container orchestration enables automatic scaling based on demand. Service mesh provides fine-grained traffic management. Caching, CDN integration, and optimized networking reduce latency. Performance is a primary design goal of cloud-native architectures.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How does cloud native prevent vendor lock-in?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Cloud-native architectures built on open standards like Kubernetes, Terraform, and Prometheus are inherently portable. Workloads can move between cloud providers, on-premises, or hybrid environments with minimal changes. The platform layer abstracts provider-specific services behind unified APIs.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you handle compliance in cloud-native environments?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Compliance is automated through policy as code, continuous audit logging, immutable infrastructure, and automated evidence collection. We implement controls for SOC 2, HIPAA, PCI DSS, FedRAMP, and GDPR using tools like OPA, Kyverno, and cloud-native audit services.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is the right cloud strategy for our organization?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">The right strategy depends on your workloads, team skills, compliance requirements, and budget. We help you evaluate single-cloud, multi-cloud, and hybrid approaches based on your specific context. There is no one-size-fits answer, and anyone who claims otherwise is selling something.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you modernize legacy monolithic applications?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">We use incremental modernization patterns. The strangler fig pattern gradually replaces monolith functionality with microservices. Parallel run validates new systems alongside old. We prioritize based on business value and risk, not technical purity.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          Will we need to retrain our engineering team?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Some upskilling is typically required. We provide structured training programs covering containers, Kubernetes, CI/CD, observability, and cloud-native development. Our goal is to make your team self-sufficient, not dependent on external consultants.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you manage cloud costs in production?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Cost management is built into the platform. We implement cost allocation tagging, budget alerts, resource right-sizing, auto-scaling policies, and scheduled shutdowns for non-production environments. FinOps practices ensure engineering and finance share cost visibility.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is GitOps and why does it matter?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">GitOps uses Git as the single source of truth for declarative infrastructure and application configuration. Cluster state automatically synchronizes with repository state. Changes are made through pull requests, reviewed, and merged. Rollbacks are simple reverts. It provides audit trail, collaboration, and consistency.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you handle secrets in Kubernetes?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Native Kubernetes secrets are base64-encoded, not encrypted. We integrate external secrets management with Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, or Azure Key Vault. Secrets are injected at runtime, never stored in version control, and automatically rotated.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is the difference between containers and VMs?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Containers share the host operating system kernel and run as isolated processes. VMs include a full guest operating system. Containers are more lightweight, start in seconds, and have higher density. VMs provide stronger isolation boundaries. Both have their place in cloud-native architectures.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How does observability differ from traditional monitoring?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Monitoring tells you when something is wrong. Observability lets you ask why. Monitoring relies on predefined dashboards and alerts. Observability provides metrics, traces, and logs that let engineers explore unknown failure modes and understand system behavior dynamically.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          Can we adopt cloud native incrementally?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Yes. Cloud-native adoption is not all-or-nothing. You can start with a single application, a new service, or a non-critical workload. We prioritize early wins that demonstrate value and build organizational confidence. Most clients adopt incrementally over 6 to 18 months.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you ensure platform governance?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Governance is codified through policy as code, resource quotas, RBAC, network policies, and approval gates in CI/CD. We establish operating models with clear ownership, API stability guarantees, versioning policies, and deprecation procedures. Governance enables, not restricts.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What happens after our engagement ends?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Your team is equipped to operate and evolve the platform independently. We provide comprehensive documentation, runbooks, and training. We offer ongoing support and advisory retainers for organizations that want continued access to our expertise.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you measure cloud-native adoption success?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">We track DORA metrics: deployment frequency, lead time, mean time to recovery, and change failure rate. Additional metrics include infrastructure cost per workload, platform adoption rate, developer satisfaction scores, and time-to-production for new services.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

